@startuml
title class diagram - WebRTCServer

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospace

class WebRTCServer {
  +host: str
  +port: int
  -_ice_config: RTCConfiguration
  -_ice_gathering_timeout: float
  -_pcs: set[RTCPeerConnection]
  -_media_relay: MediaRelay
  -_app: aiohttp.web.Application
  -_cors
  -_add_config_routes(): void
  +add_video_route(path, video_track): void
  +add_input_route(path, on_message): void
  +add_json_route(path, callback): void
  +add_offer_route(path, setup_peer): void
  +run(loop): void
  -_handle_offer(request, setup_peer): Response
  -_handle_config(request): Response
  -_wait_for_ice_gathering(pc): void
  -_on_shutdown(app): void
}

class RTCConfiguration
class RTCIceServer
class RTCPeerConnection
class RTCSessionDescription
class MediaRelay
class "aiohttp.web.Application" as AiohttpApp

class "config helpers" as Helpers {
  +ice_config_from_env(): RTCConfiguration
  +public_turn_urls_from_env(): list[str]
  +_ice_server_dict(urls): dict
  +_candidate_summary(sdp): str
}

WebRTCServer --> AiohttpApp : owns routes
WebRTCServer --> MediaRelay : shares video track
WebRTCServer --> RTCPeerConnection : creates per offer
WebRTCServer --> RTCSessionDescription : parses offer/answer
WebRTCServer --> RTCConfiguration : ICE/TURN config
RTCConfiguration *-- RTCIceServer
WebRTCServer --> Helpers : ICE and logging helpers

note bottom of WebRTCServer
  Routes:
  GET /config and /healthz
  POST /offer for video
  POST /input_offer for data channel
  GET /robot_state is added by teleop_webrtc.py
end note

@enduml
